WEBVTT

01:21.350 --> 01:23.200
You pigs watching this!

01:23.200 --> 01:24.730
I will take over your brains with my Cellphone!

01:24.730 --> 01:27.310
You shall bow before my wisdom and power!

01:45.980 --> 01:47.450
Wake up, Hubby!

01:47.450 --> 01:48.870
It's time for us to go on our honeymoon!

01:48.870 --> 01:51.380
Wake up! I said wake up!

01:51.380 --> 01:52.880
Hurry and wake up.

01:52.880 --> 01:56.140
What? Honeymoon?

01:53.260 --> 01:54.460
Let's go. Let's go.

01:56.840 --> 01:59.010
You still haven't given up on it?

01:59.010 --> 02:00.300
Obviously not.

02:00.300 --> 02:02.140
Look at this!

02:04.960 --> 02:06.340
What is this?

02:06.340 --> 02:07.730
A runway.

02:07.730 --> 02:11.500
It's a pain to go to the airport, so I had it come to me.

02:11.500 --> 02:12.690
"Had it come to me..."

02:12.690 --> 02:13.640
When did she do this?

02:12.980 --> 02:15.980
Where did all the neighbors go?

02:13.640 --> 02:14.740
As expected of Kitty.

02:14.740 --> 02:15.980
I'm simply amazed.

02:15.980 --> 02:18.490
Good. I'm glad you're quick to comprehend.

02:18.490 --> 02:20.160
Don't tell me you...

02:20.160 --> 02:22.130
Leave the details out.

02:22.130 --> 02:24.240
You all, too. Thank you for your cooperation.

02:37.700 --> 02:40.340
Off we go to the honeymoon everyone dreams of!

02:40.340 --> 02:42.080
Yay!

02:46.890 --> 02:48.050
It's very quiet.

02:48.770 --> 02:51.180
No stands or beach houses.

02:51.180 --> 02:53.110
It's an uninhabited island, so I wouldn't expect any of that.

02:53.110 --> 02:55.600
Can't see anyone swimming, either.

02:55.600 --> 02:57.770
It's an uninhabited island, so I wouldn't expect any of that.

02:57.770 --> 03:00.740
In other words, this beach is the Midarezaki private beach.

03:00.740 --> 03:03.140
It's an uninhabited island, so- Wait, hold on!

03:03.140 --> 03:06.350
You don't have a sense of guilt after doing that, Kyouka?

03:06.350 --> 03:09.660
I have yet to feel that in my life.

03:09.660 --> 03:14.210
It's that plane's fault for not being able
to keep up with my amazing aerial maneuvers.

03:14.210 --> 03:17.270
You didn't look like you were able to pilot at all.

03:17.270 --> 03:20.840
I, Kyouka-sama, am a prodigy who learned how to ride a bike in only two months!

03:20.840 --> 03:22.890
Bike? Two months?

03:25.720 --> 03:26.640
Hi.

03:26.640 --> 03:29.310
Whee! Dad! Mom!

03:29.310 --> 03:31.540
Yuuka! Hyouka!

03:31.980 --> 03:34.710
I've checked what it's like from the sky.

03:34.710 --> 03:36.360
All other family members are unhurt.

03:36.360 --> 03:37.850
So they're safe.

03:38.260 --> 03:39.820
Did you get hurt at all?

03:39.820 --> 03:42.970
No. I'm simply okay thanks to Hyouka.

03:42.970 --> 03:44.910
I didn't know Hyouka could even fly.

03:44.910 --> 03:49.510
That's right! Hyouka can blast the fart he's been holding for months and fly.

03:49.510 --> 03:50.910
Praise modern science!

03:50.910 --> 03:52.670
Don't make up things.

03:52.670 --> 03:54.630
It's nothing that special.

03:55.120 --> 03:56.090
Look.

03:56.090 --> 03:57.460
Oh, this is...

03:57.460 --> 03:58.670
It's beautiful.

03:58.670 --> 03:59.620
It's Levistone.

03:59.620 --> 04:01.950
The professor who created me called it that.

04:01.950 --> 04:07.200
If a certain amount of electricity is passed through, it ignores gravity and levitates objects.

04:05.270 --> 04:07.200
Hey, Kitty!

04:07.760 --> 04:10.860
With ten kilograms of this stuff,
I think an entire island could be levitated.

04:07.760 --> 04:09.680
We're over here.

04:10.110 --> 04:12.060
I'm totally soaked.

04:12.060 --> 04:13.280
Everyone.

04:13.280 --> 04:14.250
Thank goodness.

04:14.250 --> 04:16.030
Looks like we're all back together.

04:16.030 --> 04:16.860
And now!

04:17.610 --> 04:19.690
Time for a swim!

04:19.690 --> 04:21.150
Yeah!

04:25.520 --> 04:27.120
Wait, Honored Sister.

04:27.120 --> 04:28.700
Follow me, Teika-kun.

04:28.700 --> 04:32.700
Now, Ginichi-san. Let me lecture you on how wonderful girls are.

04:32.700 --> 04:35.870
Help me! My character's going to get destroyed!

04:35.870 --> 04:37.330
Harden it. Harden it.

04:39.240 --> 04:42.150
Looks like everyone's having some fun, but...

04:43.340 --> 04:45.200
Is it really all right for us to be doing this?

04:45.680 --> 04:47.650
What's with that gloomy face?

04:47.650 --> 04:50.930
Do you have a problem with a honeymoon with your beautiful wife?

04:50.930 --> 04:54.350
You even prepared a beachball. How very well prepared.

04:55.640 --> 04:58.870
Since we're here, it's a waste if you don't enjoy it.

04:58.870 --> 05:00.150
Just the two of us on the white beach.

05:00.150 --> 05:02.710
Come on, catch me if you can.

05:02.120 --> 05:03.500
I'm going to arrest you.

05:04.240 --> 05:07.030
Please don't have such a disgusting illusion, Honey.

05:07.030 --> 05:09.490
If you need to bleed out of your nose,
do so without hesitation.

05:09.490 --> 05:15.250
It's your right as husband to get to see me in a swimsuit, when even the spirits of summer run away barefooted.

05:15.250 --> 05:17.290
Yes, yes. You're very cute, Kyouka.

05:17.290 --> 05:20.590
Do you really love Kyouka-sama herself?

05:21.420 --> 05:25.010
At the very least, I'm making an effort to love you!

05:25.010 --> 05:27.280
Do you not see that?

05:27.680 --> 05:30.760
I'm incapable of loving someone.

05:31.340 --> 05:35.170
Even so, I do care about the family.

05:35.170 --> 05:38.310
Plus, I do like you.

05:41.770 --> 05:44.610
Did you not see that?

05:46.610 --> 05:49.530
I knew it. I was just worried for a second.

05:50.110 --> 05:52.620
Since I do get hung up sometimes.

06:01.420 --> 06:03.380
I'm so hungry.

06:03.380 --> 06:05.170
I'm so tired.

06:05.170 --> 06:09.380
We need to find some food and a place to sleep fast, or else we'll be in danger.

06:09.380 --> 06:14.630
It's crazy to play around and waste energy on an uninhabited island.

06:14.630 --> 06:15.940
Stop yapping.

06:15.940 --> 06:17.150
Don't worry.

06:17.150 --> 06:21.740
According to this pamphlet, we'll arrive at the hotel if we keep going straight.

06:21.740 --> 06:22.670
Pamphlet?

06:22.670 --> 06:23.690
Hotel?

06:26.880 --> 06:28.610
There, I found it. It's right here.

06:32.620 --> 06:34.580
Why's a hotel at a place like this?

06:35.540 --> 06:36.890
It's beyond suspicious.

06:36.890 --> 06:39.290
Kyouka, what are you planning?

06:39.290 --> 06:42.040
"Plan"? I don't have a clue.

06:42.040 --> 06:44.820
Show me that pamphlet in your hand.

06:44.820 --> 06:47.800
Shut up. Those who do not believe the god's words shall be punished.

06:45.980 --> 06:46.810
Hey!

06:47.320 --> 06:49.300
Please stop fighting!

06:53.480 --> 06:54.790
Ow...

06:55.180 --> 06:57.560
I fell over again.

06:58.040 --> 07:01.400
Welcome to Chokokutou Riverside Hotel.

07:01.400 --> 07:05.150
You must be the Midarezaki who made the reservation, right?

07:05.150 --> 07:08.700
Yes! Those you see here are the followers of the god!

07:08.700 --> 07:09.780
The Midarezaki!

07:09.780 --> 07:10.700
Reservations?

07:11.890 --> 07:13.210
I should have known.

07:13.210 --> 07:22.270
The hotel's motto is "relief, safety, and peace," and we make daily efforts to ensure our customers enjoy their stay.

07:20.440 --> 07:22.270
It's delicious!

07:22.710 --> 07:26.710
Please enjoy your four days of vacation here.

07:26.710 --> 07:28.650
It's so delicious.

07:28.650 --> 07:29.300
Exquisite.

07:29.300 --> 07:31.590
Ginichi-san, say ah.

07:31.590 --> 07:32.710
Itadakimasu.

07:32.710 --> 07:34.360
Have some of this, too.

07:36.080 --> 07:36.920
It's good!

07:36.920 --> 07:43.400
Be happy! To satisfy my tongue gives you
the ticket to be in history textbooks, Pierre.

07:43.400 --> 07:45.240
P-Pierre?

07:45.240 --> 07:49.150
No, I'm this hotel's manager, Nishikura Akeru.

07:49.150 --> 07:55.000
Don't you know the universal law that says anyone wearing a white tux and a red bowtie is to be called Pierre?

07:55.000 --> 07:57.520
Besides, your name isn't funny at all.

07:57.520 --> 07:59.450
Refer to yourself as Nishikura Pierre starting today!

08:00.240 --> 08:00.950
Um...

08:00.950 --> 08:03.580
I'm simply full.

08:03.580 --> 08:05.420
May I have some water, Pierre-san?

08:05.420 --> 08:07.150
Like I said, I'm...

08:07.150 --> 08:09.130
Let's write it down so no one makes any mistake.

08:09.720 --> 08:12.130
Scribble, scribble, scribble.

08:12.130 --> 08:17.890
Scribble: Pierre

08:12.130 --> 08:15.480
You're now Pierre no matter who sees you.

08:15.480 --> 08:17.930
How could you! This jacket was very expensive.

08:18.980 --> 08:20.790
You're so mean!

08:19.900 --> 08:21.680
What is she doing...

08:21.190 --> 08:22.610
More trouble, again...

08:27.770 --> 08:30.070
It must be hard for you.

08:30.610 --> 08:33.440
I don't see any other staff here.

08:33.440 --> 08:35.170
Are you managing this big hotel alone?

08:35.170 --> 08:36.030
Yes.

08:36.030 --> 08:39.410
But, because of that, I feel that it's a very worthwhile job.

08:39.830 --> 08:42.040
Thank you for your concern.

08:42.040 --> 08:44.160
The dinner was very delicious.

08:44.160 --> 08:47.690
I-It was nothing out of the ordinary.

08:47.690 --> 08:51.790
Who knows what would have happened to me if Kyouka-sama hadn't come here.

08:51.790 --> 08:52.420
Kyouka?

08:53.310 --> 08:54.300
No, um...

08:54.300 --> 08:56.770
That was a slip of the tongue. Please forget it.

08:56.770 --> 09:01.680
It's fine, Nishikura-san. I'm sure my wife forced an unreasonable task upon you, right?

09:01.680 --> 09:03.660
No, absolutely not!

09:03.660 --> 09:07.460
If it wasn't for her, we wouldn't have seen a runway built overnight,

09:07.460 --> 09:09.100
or had the plane we got on crash,

09:09.100 --> 09:13.030
or found an amazing hotel like this on an island we accidentally drifted to.

09:13.980 --> 09:15.450
Ouka-sama, then...

09:15.450 --> 09:20.950
It looks like we've caused some trouble to the people at the Paranormal Phenomena Bureau of Measures again.

09:20.950 --> 09:23.080
To think you've figured all that out...

09:23.770 --> 09:29.830
I am from Paranormal Phenomena Bureau of Measures, 2nd Research Department, Nishikura Akeru.

09:30.250 --> 09:32.180
I was having an inkling of that.

09:32.180 --> 09:38.200
I wasn't blessed with any talent in the lab, so I always slowed everyone down, and there wasn't a place for me.

09:38.200 --> 09:46.420
But thanks to this trip, I was able to take on a new mission where I get to take care of everyone here at Chokokutou.

09:46.420 --> 09:50.350
I can't even find words of gratitude for Kyouka-sama, who planned this trip.

09:51.180 --> 09:53.150
She even gave me this wonderful nickname.

09:53.150 --> 09:55.240
Oh, so you actually liked it.

09:56.050 --> 09:57.280
So, Nishikura-san.

09:57.280 --> 09:58.150
What exactly is this island?

09:58.150 --> 10:02.670
It's an island located at the southernmost edge of the Great Japanese Empire.

10:02.670 --> 10:04.040
Chokokutou Island.

10:04.770 --> 10:13.710
The name comes from how the natives that used to live here called the island an "island where birds cry".

10:14.210 --> 10:18.720
Some professor who decoded their writing gave the name.

10:18.720 --> 10:20.380
Island where birds cry...

10:20.800 --> 10:22.220
Chokokutou, is it...

10:22.220 --> 10:24.260
But please don't worry.

10:24.260 --> 10:33.140
Before you arrived, all large animals, birds, reptiles, dangerous insects, and microbes were eliminated.

10:33.820 --> 10:39.610
Chokokutou is now the world's safest,
most peaceful untouched piece of nature.

10:40.150 --> 10:42.870
I sense a contradiction there.

10:43.340 --> 10:47.690
Since you've come, please enjoy your vacation, Ouka-sama.

10:48.490 --> 10:50.250
Yes. But...

10:50.250 --> 10:54.610
I'm sure your family would be happier that way, too.

10:55.010 --> 10:55.720
Eh?

10:55.720 --> 10:56.760
I'm...

10:56.790 --> 10:57.800
So fluffy!

10:58.880 --> 10:59.920
So silky.

11:00.800 --> 11:01.970
Adults are...

11:01.970 --> 11:07.500
I'm very envious of Ouka-sama, since you're surrounded by such a wonderful family.

11:07.500 --> 11:09.270
I guess.

11:11.530 --> 11:14.500
The bath is to the left.

11:14.500 --> 11:16.140
Please enjoy.

11:21.760 --> 11:24.580
Must hurry. Our master's death is close.

11:25.570 --> 11:28.680
However, we can't cure his illness.

11:28.680 --> 11:31.970
Mortals, our targets are the small girls.

11:31.970 --> 11:34.430
For our great master! For our great god!

11:34.430 --> 11:35.880
Please wait.

11:35.880 --> 11:38.120
We'll soon bring you a sacrifice.

11:47.180 --> 11:49.810
Father... Mother...

12:19.940 --> 12:24.010
Ouka-san, why are you thinking of something that makes you want to die just from pondering it?

12:27.260 --> 12:30.830
He might have had a family or a beloved person.

12:30.830 --> 12:34.740
It's all a trap set by God. The infinite Hell.

12:34.740 --> 12:36.880
Does it not hurt you, Grim Reaper?

12:37.600 --> 12:38.800
To kill so much...

12:38.800 --> 12:42.910
It's pointless for you to wish me to share your sense of vanity.

12:42.910 --> 12:46.320
But I think you're fine that way, Ouka-san.

12:46.320 --> 12:48.200
If you were to become a Grim Reaper,

12:48.700 --> 12:51.450
I would destroy your face.

12:58.460 --> 12:59.240
An alarm?

12:59.880 --> 13:00.840
What is going on?

13:03.690 --> 13:04.740
Hyouka.

13:04.740 --> 13:06.130
Father, we might have some trouble.

13:06.130 --> 13:08.300
This building is under attack.

13:08.300 --> 13:10.880
Power is completely shut down.

13:10.880 --> 13:14.180
Judging from the footsteps, they are a party of greater than twenty.

13:14.680 --> 13:15.930
Their identity is unknown.

13:15.930 --> 13:17.810
They'll soon be up to the second floor.

13:17.810 --> 13:18.730
To here?

13:19.080 --> 13:20.150
What are Yuuka and Chika-san doing?

13:20.150 --> 13:22.660
Father, can I fight?

13:23.240 --> 13:24.490
Can I go wild?

13:24.490 --> 13:25.490
Can I destroy?

13:25.490 --> 13:26.460
Can I kill?

13:26.460 --> 13:27.610
You mustn't, Hyouka.

13:27.610 --> 13:29.320
Why? They're the enemy.

13:29.320 --> 13:31.190
We'll be killed if we don't kill.

13:31.190 --> 13:32.370
I want to fight.

13:32.370 --> 13:35.870
Are you confident you'll kill the enemy and only the enemy?

13:35.870 --> 13:40.880
Can you swear that you will not lose control of yourself from the ecstasy of fighting and kill a family member?

13:41.460 --> 13:43.740
You're no longer a biological weapon.

13:43.740 --> 13:45.910
You mustn't turn into a grim reaper.

13:45.910 --> 13:47.000
Okay.

13:47.000 --> 13:49.720
But Father, if we're not going to fight, what do we do?

13:49.720 --> 13:51.600
There's only one choice.

13:51.600 --> 13:52.180
We run.

13:53.510 --> 13:58.770
You work with Teika and Gekka and run, protecting Yuuka and the others.

13:58.770 --> 13:59.610
What will you do?

13:59.610 --> 14:03.570
I'll start out by punishing the cause of this event.

14:04.900 --> 14:06.690
I see.

14:09.950 --> 14:11.940
So this is what a love comedy is. How very intriguing!

14:11.940 --> 14:15.870
It's a wonderful form of information that contains men's desires!

14:15.870 --> 14:17.710
Ah, Ouka, you pervert!

14:17.710 --> 14:21.100
Oh, I'm sorry, Kyouka.
I didn't know you were taking a shower.

14:21.100 --> 14:24.010
Kyouka-sama falls to her knees from shame and starts to cry.

14:24.010 --> 14:29.970
Ouka doesn't know it's an act and softens from the sense of guilt for seeing the equivalent of a goddess' naked body.

14:29.970 --> 14:32.610
I'll do anything if you'll forgive me.

14:32.610 --> 14:33.640
Do you mean it?

14:34.030 --> 14:39.140
Then I want Eurasia ♥

14:44.050 --> 14:47.230
What do you think you're doing, sneaking into a girl's room in the middle of the night?!

14:49.990 --> 14:53.420
He saw my embarrassing secret.

14:53.420 --> 14:54.740
Ouka, you jerk.

14:54.740 --> 14:56.240
You're the jerk!

14:56.240 --> 15:00.040
Castaway on an uninhabited island isn't enough? What are you planning now?!

15:00.040 --> 15:02.850
What are you so angry about?

15:02.850 --> 15:07.040
I only tried framing you in a love-comedy-like development and haven't done anything yet.

15:08.010 --> 15:09.730
W-What is this noise?

15:10.030 --> 15:11.540
You didn't notice?

15:11.540 --> 15:16.580
I was planning on watching ridiculously idiotic late-night anime with some beer and then going to bed when I got sleepy!

15:16.580 --> 15:17.390
So I don't have a clue about this!

15:17.390 --> 15:19.040
Then this ruckus is...

15:20.020 --> 15:20.690
Yuuka!

15:20.690 --> 15:21.690
It's outside!

15:24.500 --> 15:25.240
Yuuka!

15:30.150 --> 15:31.460
What are they?

15:32.170 --> 15:33.160
Monkeys?

15:33.160 --> 15:34.910
Mom! Dad!

15:35.550 --> 15:36.470
Yuuka!

15:36.470 --> 15:38.460
You dare kidnap the god's daughter?

15:38.460 --> 15:40.310
I take it that you guys don't value your lives.

15:42.580 --> 15:43.330
What?

15:45.920 --> 15:46.340
Kyouka!

15:46.790 --> 15:48.720
PLACEHOLDER

15:46.790 --> 15:49.390
It feels disgusting!

15:48.720 --> 15:51.000
Are you all right, Kyouka?

15:49.390 --> 15:51.000
Drop me!

15:51.000 --> 15:52.480
How impudent of them...

15:52.480 --> 15:53.620
You can't move.

15:53.620 --> 15:56.430
Our daughter is about to get kidnapped. This is nothing.

15:57.510 --> 15:58.140
What?

16:01.430 --> 16:04.430
"Great master"? Who is that?

16:06.470 --> 16:08.780
Mom! Dad!

16:08.780 --> 16:10.570
Stop!

16:10.570 --> 16:10.900
Wait.

16:13.070 --> 16:14.090
Yuuka! Yuuka!

16:14.090 --> 16:16.570
Mom! Dad!

16:16.570 --> 16:17.780
This can't be...

16:18.660 --> 16:20.780
Yuuka!

16:27.300 --> 16:28.830
Where is this place?

16:28.830 --> 16:30.920
Dad... Mom...

16:30.920 --> 16:32.880
What's going to happen to me?

16:33.210 --> 16:35.690
I won't get to see everyone again?

16:36.050 --> 16:39.480
Save me, Mom, Dad.

16:39.480 --> 16:43.420
Nee-sama. Ginka-san. Teika-kun. Hyouka.

16:44.040 --> 16:45.000
Gekka?

16:45.940 --> 16:47.430
You came for me!

16:47.430 --> 16:49.130
Good girl.

16:47.920 --> 16:50.400
Ah, you simply made me slimy.

16:50.400 --> 16:52.780
Are you telling me not to worry?

16:59.470 --> 17:00.450
What do you mean?

17:08.800 --> 17:13.070
So, Nishikura-san, even you don't have a clue what those monkeys are.

17:13.070 --> 17:18.550
No. I can swear to the Emperor of the Great Japanese Empire that I don't know anything about them.

17:18.550 --> 17:21.460
Professional research groups have come to investigate this place three times,

17:21.460 --> 17:25.560
so there's no chance wild animals like them could be here.

17:25.560 --> 17:28.290
But the huge monkeys do exist.

17:28.290 --> 17:29.440
And now Yuuka is...

17:29.440 --> 17:33.900
I'm sorry Father. It's because we took time saving Chika.

17:33.900 --> 17:35.280
I'm at fault, as well.

17:35.280 --> 17:38.700
No, there's no reason for you to feel responsible.

17:38.700 --> 17:41.610
There's evidence that shows they headed directly to Yuuka's room.

17:41.610 --> 17:44.420
So they were only after Yuuka-chan to begin with?

17:44.420 --> 17:45.410
That would be the case.

17:45.410 --> 17:49.180
You're keeping it cool and running analysis in a situation like this? I'm amazed!

17:49.180 --> 17:50.590
What exactly do you mean by that?

17:50.590 --> 17:53.260
This is a challenge against us Midarezaki.

17:53.260 --> 17:55.060
That's all we need to know.

17:55.060 --> 17:56.590
Then we'll accept it!

17:56.590 --> 17:57.970
What do you plan on doing?

17:57.970 --> 18:01.350
We save Yuuka and destroy them without any mercy.

18:01.350 --> 18:02.940
With that wound you have?

18:03.330 --> 18:06.110
Even your power was meaningless to them.

18:06.110 --> 18:09.190
I don't think charging in is a good idea.

18:09.190 --> 18:12.610
Ouka. Were you born from a robot's loins?

18:13.860 --> 18:16.090
Our precious daughter was kidnapped!

18:16.090 --> 18:17.490
Why should I care about myself?!

18:17.490 --> 18:19.680
To fight even if an arm is lost or guts are ripped out.

18:19.680 --> 18:20.990
That's what parents are for!

18:20.990 --> 18:22.450
B-But...

18:22.450 --> 18:27.180
If you can't get into a frenzy when a family member is in danger, then you're no human!

18:27.580 --> 18:32.670
I'm not like that. If it means saving my daughter, I'll create all the miracles I need!

18:32.670 --> 18:33.750
That's what parents are!

18:33.750 --> 18:35.130
What humans are!

18:35.130 --> 18:36.460
But, Kitty.

18:36.460 --> 18:40.220
We don't even know where Yuuka-chan is right now.

18:40.610 --> 18:43.190
Chika, do you know what creates miracles?

18:43.190 --> 18:44.360
God!

18:44.360 --> 18:45.440
The pinnacle of all things!

18:45.440 --> 18:46.940
The law that governs destiny!

18:46.940 --> 18:48.650
The Kyouka-sama you see right here!

18:49.270 --> 18:51.300
Have you forgotten my divine power?

18:51.300 --> 18:53.110
Sit there and observe.

18:54.770 --> 19:00.070
That's right. Kitty has an irregular,
yet convenient, skill called Cellphone.

19:04.690 --> 19:05.610
Mother?

19:07.600 --> 19:08.750
Can't connect yet?

19:08.750 --> 19:12.320
Hold on. Yuuka isn't very opinionated, so it's hard to find her.

19:12.320 --> 19:14.250
But I will find her.

19:14.620 --> 19:15.550
Kyouka...

19:16.030 --> 19:17.840
Hey, stupid daughter, do you hear me?

19:17.840 --> 19:19.510
If you hear me, then answer.

19:21.470 --> 19:22.720
Is that you, Mom?

19:22.720 --> 19:26.600
Oh, thank goodness! I'm right here!

19:27.670 --> 19:29.220
So you're alive.

19:29.220 --> 19:32.890
So you were searching for me. I was simply trusting you.

19:32.890 --> 19:36.630
Yes, but we need you to work, too, until we get to meet again.

19:36.630 --> 19:39.060
I'm going to steal your sight for a second.

19:39.060 --> 19:40.460
My sight?

19:40.460 --> 19:41.320
Steal?

19:43.890 --> 19:47.910
Yuuka. Right now, I'm seeing exactly what you're seeing.

19:47.910 --> 19:51.110
What is this? Looks like you're getting quite a welcome there.

19:51.110 --> 19:52.570
Yup. It tastes great.

19:52.570 --> 19:53.400
That's good.

19:53.400 --> 19:54.980
No! Don't eat without any caution!

19:54.980 --> 19:56.630
Anyway, staying there won't get us anywhere.

19:56.630 --> 19:59.550
Get out of there and find something that'll help us locate you.

19:59.550 --> 20:01.200
Get out of this room?

20:01.530 --> 20:03.480
Okay, Mom.

20:03.480 --> 20:04.420
Be careful.

20:05.050 --> 20:08.480
I'll be fine. I'm your daughter, after all.

20:10.110 --> 20:12.560
Um... Um... Um...

20:12.560 --> 20:14.620
I'd like to go to the bathroom.

20:15.560 --> 20:18.150
By the way, that was me falling.

20:18.150 --> 20:20.860
Will such an overused trick work?!

20:23.170 --> 20:24.450
It's that way?

20:24.450 --> 20:26.440
Simply thank you, monkeys.

20:29.250 --> 20:30.660
They're so kind.

20:30.660 --> 20:32.540
Works well for us.

20:35.370 --> 20:38.040
Who was it that sent the telepathic message?

20:38.040 --> 20:40.680
Must be the supporter of the princess who we're giving to our master.

20:40.680 --> 20:42.770
That fearsome non-human brat.

20:42.770 --> 20:44.460
The princess might run away.

20:44.460 --> 20:46.250
There won't be any interference to our project.

20:46.250 --> 20:47.890
Only that room is at the end of the hall.

20:47.890 --> 20:50.970
Everything is going well without any problems.

20:50.970 --> 20:52.290
It's all for our great master.

20:53.880 --> 20:54.920
It's a window.

20:54.920 --> 20:57.160
You might be able to get out through that.

20:57.160 --> 20:58.480
Yeah, I'll take a look.

21:01.210 --> 21:02.490
Up I go.

21:06.200 --> 21:07.070
You're joking...

21:16.400 --> 21:20.290
I see. No wonder the research groups never found them.

21:20.710 --> 21:22.330
What do you see?

21:22.330 --> 21:23.260
Kitty?

21:23.260 --> 21:28.260
A castle in the sky protected by multiple monkeys, I guess.

21:29.830 --> 21:33.640
Yuuka, you're caught in a very interesting place.

21:33.640 --> 21:35.390
No, I don't want this.

21:41.150 --> 21:42.320
This is...

21:42.320 --> 21:43.780
You mustn't touch that stone!

21:45.670 --> 21:46.890
Who is it?

21:53.950 --> 21:56.330
A small monkey?

21:56.330 --> 21:58.170
H-How rude of you.

21:58.170 --> 21:59.720
I'm human!

21:59.720 --> 22:01.920
Oh, I'm sorry.

22:01.920 --> 22:03.340
Would you like to have a banana?

22:21.660 --> 22:24.150
Have you recharged your will,
perseverance, carefreeness, and energy?

22:24.150 --> 22:26.450
I'll give you another minute and a half of frenzy.

22:26.450 --> 22:27.730
Are you ready for this? Here I go!

23:40.570 --> 23:41.640
This is Yuuka.

23:41.640 --> 23:43.610
I'm at an island to the south right now.

23:43.610 --> 23:46.320
I came here with everyone in the family.

23:46.320 --> 23:48.890
I'll be fine, right?

23:48.890 --> 23:50.110
Mom...

23:50.790 --> 23:53.910
Next time: Insane Professor and Double the Party.
